AndroWish's PendingIntents name their mutability.

Android 12 (API 31) refuses a PendingIntent that says neither
FLAG_IMMUTABLE nor FLAG_MUTABLE: the call throws, and the borg command
behind it does nothing — a notification never posts, an alarm never
sets, an SMS's sent/delivered callbacks never come. The app targets
API 36. Immutable wherever the intent is complete as built; mutable
for NFC and USB, where the system fills in extras. Applied after
notification-channel.patch.

